= Dawen Liang 

~~~
{}{img_left}{files/dawen.jpg}{Dawen Liang}{124}{140} \n
Email: {{<img src="files/email.png" alt="email address" width="150" style="vertical-align: middle;">}} \n

I am a machine learning researcher at [https://openai.com/ OpenAI]. Previously I worked at [https://x.ai/ xAI] and [https://www.netflix.com/ Netflix], focusing on LLM post-training, policy learning, and personalization. I completed my Ph.D. in the [https://www.ee.columbia.edu/ Electrical
Engineering Department] at [https://www.columbia.edu/ Columbia University],
as part of the [http://labrosa.ee.columbia.edu LabROSA],
working with [https://www.ee.columbia.edu/~dpwe/ Professor Dan
Ellis] and [https://www.cs.columbia.edu/~blei/ Professor David Blei].
Prior to that, I completed my master's degree in
[https://www.cmu.edu/cfa/music/programs/graduate-programs/grad-music-technology.html Music and Technology program] at
[https://www.cmu.edu/index.shtml Carnegie Mellon University], working with
[https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~rbd Professor Roger Dannenberg] in the
[https://www.cs.cmu.edu School of Computer Science], where I was part of the
[https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~music/ Computer Music Group].
~~~

== Publications

For the most up-to-date information, please see my [https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=4c1ZNm4AAAAJ&hl=en Google Scholar] page.


== Miscellaneous
Here are some old notes on topics I once spent time learning about. They unfortunately become increasingly irrelevant in the current age of LLMs, but I keep them here as a small piece of technical nostalgia. I hope they may still be useful to someone, though they may contain mistakes or outdated information. If you notice any problems, please let me know.

- [files/mle_biased.pdf A proof] that Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) is
  biased for variance estimator.
- [files/mat_deriv.pdf A note] that shows some useful properties for matrix
  derivative.
- [files/em.pdf Some technical details] for the Expectation Maximization (EM)
  algorithm.
